<title>MALAYSIA: Malaysia opposition figure convicted of sedition.</title>
<headline>Malaysia opposition figure convicted of sedition.</headline>
<dateline>MALACCA, Malaysia 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Malaysian high court in the west coast city of Malacca found an opposition member of parliament guilty of sedition on Monday.</p>
<p>Lim Guan Eng, the youth leader of the Democratic Action Party, was fined a total of 15,000 ringgit ($5,976) on two charges of sedition and spreading false news and will lose his seat in parliament as a result.</p>
</text>
